{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Syncable","kind":"identifier"},{"text":" : AnyObject","kind":"text"}]}]},{"mentions":["doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/GettingStarted"],"kind":"mentions"},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Global identifiers let Ensembles recognize when objects created independently","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"on different devices represent the same logical entity, and merge them instead","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of duplicating.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"There are two ways to provide a global identifier:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Simple: Single Property","anchor":"Simple-Single-Property","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Override ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/Syncable\/globalIdentifierKey","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" with the name of a stored property:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ Core Data","class Note: NSManagedObject, Syncable {","    static let globalIdentifierKey = \"uniqueID\"","    @NSManaged var uniqueID: String","}","","\/\/ SwiftData","@Model","class Tag: Syncable {","    static let globalIdentifierKey = \"name\"","    var name: String","}"]},{"type":"heading","text":"Advanced: Computed Identifier (Core Data)","level":3,"anchor":"Advanced-Computed-Identifier-Core-Data"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Override "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/Syncable\/globalIdentifier(from:)"},{"type":"text","text":" for compound or computed identifiers."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The parameter is typed as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self"},{"type":"text","text":", so you get direct property access:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["class Person: NSManagedObject, Syncable {","    @NSManaged var firstName: String","    @NSManaged var lastName: String","","    static func globalIdentifier(from person: Person) -> String {","        \"\\(person.firstName).\\(person.lastName)\"","    }","}"]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/Syncable\/globalIdentifier(from:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" only works with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSManagedObject"},{"type":"text","text":" subclasses"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(Core Data). For SwiftData models, use "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/Syncable\/globalIdentifierKey","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" instead."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside","name":"Note","style":"note"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A global identifier "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"must never change","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" once it has been assigned"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to an object. Changing an identifier after sync has begun will cause Ensembles"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to treat the object as a different entity, leading to duplicates or data loss."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Use a value that is set once at creation time, such as a UUID string."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside","name":"Important","style":"important"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A UUID is usually the best choice for a global identifier. Use a fixed,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"meaningful value (like a name) only for singleton objects or reference data"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"like tags, where two devices might independently create the same logical object."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When model types conform to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Syncable"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsembleContainer","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiftDataEnsembleContainer"},{"text":" discover the identifiers automatically — no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"delegate or closure needed.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:9Ensembles8SyncableP","modules":[{"name":"Ensembles"}],"symbolKind":"protocol","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Syncable","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"Syncable","roleHeading":"Protocol","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Syncable","kind":"identifier"}]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ensembles\/syncable"]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles"]]},"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Type-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/Syncable\/globalIdentifierKey"],"title":"Type Properties"},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Type-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/Syncable\/globalIdentifier(from:)"],"title":"Type Methods"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/Syncable"},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"A protocol for model types that declare how to derive a global identifier","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for Ensembles deduplication.","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://